{"id":"tv-0433","task_type": "data_analysis", "complexity": "medium","prompt":"We migrated the warehouse loader to the new scheduler last month and my manager keeps pinging me about the cost report, and I\u0027ve also been on call since Monday running on about three hours of sleep, but what I actually need from you is to go through this log excerpt from the last three nights and quantify per job how often retries, upstream wait time and late starts occurred and which dependency chain accounts for most of the SLA misses.\n\n2031-03-04 01:02:11 INFO job=ingest_clicks start sla=03:00\n2031-03-04 01:40:52 WARN job=ingest_clicks upstream=raw_events_export wait=2310s\n2031-03-04 02:15:09 INFO job=ingest_clicks retry=1 reason=lock_timeout\n2031-03-04 03:22:40 ERROR job=build_sessions sla_missed=true late_by=1320s upstream=ingest_clicks\n2031-03-05 01:01:58 INFO job=ingest_clicks start sla=03:00\n2031-03-05 01:05:20 INFO job=ingest_clicks upstream=raw_events_export wait=190s\n2031-03-05 02:48:33 INFO job=build_sessions start sla=04:00\n2031-03-05 03:59:12 INFO job=daily_revenue start late_by=0s upstream=build_sessions\n2031-03-06 01:03:02 WARN job=ingest_clicks upstream=raw_events_export wait=3050s\n2031-03-06 02:30:47 INFO job=ingest_clicks retry=1 reason=lock_timeout\n2031-03-06 02:51:10 INFO job=ingest_clicks retry=2 reason=lock_timeout\n2031-03-06 04:41:25 ERROR job=build_sessions sla_missed=true late_by=2485s upstream=ingest_clicks\n2031-03-06 05:30:01 ERROR job=daily_revenue sla_missed=true late_by=3600s upstream=build_sessions"}
