{"id":"tv-0031","task_type": "code_generation", "complexity": "low","prompt":"Could you extend this script so that it groups pods by namespace and writes a CSV with the namespace, pod name and total container restart count, sorted by restarts in descending order?\n\n```python\nfrom kubernetes import client, config\n\nconfig.load_kube_config()\nv1 = client.CoreV1Api()\n\npods = v1.list_pod_for_all_namespaces().items\nfor p in pods:\n    print(p.metadata.namespace, p.metadata.name)\n```"}
{"id":"tv-0144","task_type": "", "complexity": "","prompt":"One of our API deployments stopped autoscaling after we added a logging sidecar last week. The HPA shows `\u003cunknown\u003e/70%` for CPU, and its events say it failed to compute utilization for the pod. Here is the relevant part of the Deployment and the HPA. Can you work out what is wrong and show me the corrected manifests?\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: orders-api\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: orders-api\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: orders-api\n    spec:\n      containers:\n        - name: api\n          image: registry.internal/orders-api:2.14.0\n          resources:\n            requests:\n              cpu: 250m\n              memory: 256Mi\n        - name: log-shipper\n          image: registry.internal/log-shipper:1.3.2\n          resources:\n            limits:\n              memory: 128Mi\n---\napiVersion: autoscaling/v2\nkind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler\nmetadata:\n  name: orders-api\nspec:\n  scaleTargetRef:\n    apiVersion: apps/v1\n    kind: Deployment\n    name: orders-api\n  minReplicas: 3\n  maxReplicas: 12\n  metrics:\n    - type: Resource\n      resource:\n        name: cpu\n        target:\n          type: Utilization\n          averageUtilization: 70\n```"}
{"id":"tv-0122","task_type": "", "complexity": "","prompt":"So last weekend I finally got my old mechanical keyboard working again, and now I am finally back to building the React dashboard for our reports team. The Python backend is FastAPI and I use `allow_origins=[\"*\"]` in CORSMiddleware because I wanted it to be easy while developing. When I log in and call `fetch(\u0027http://localhost:8000/api/reports\u0027, {credentials: \u0027include\u0027})` from my Vite app on port 5173 I get: \"Access to fetch at \u0027http://localhost:8000/api/reports\u0027 from origin \u0027http://localhost:5173\u0027 has been blocked by CORS policy: The value of the \u0027Access-Control-Allow-Origin\u0027 header in the response must not be the wildcard \u0027*\u0027 when the request\u0027s credentials mode is \u0027include\u0027.\" It works fine from curl and Postman, so how do I fix the backend so the session cookie goes through in the browser?"}
{"id":"tv-0315","task_type": "", "complexity": "","prompt":"hey, i wrote this migration guide for moving our terraform state from local files to the s3 backend but its messy and my lead said its hard to follow. can you rewrite it so its clear step by step, with a short before you start checklist and a section for what to do if something goes wrong. keep my content and dont add steps i didnt mention, if you think somthing important is missing just flag it at the end\n\nmy draft:\n\nso first you need to make sure nobody else is running terraform at the same time, just tell in the channel. then go to the folder of your stack and make a backup of terraform.tfstate, i usually copy it to a bak file. after that edit backend.tf and add the s3 block with bucket name tf-state-platform-dev and the key which should be the folder name plus terraform.tfstate. region is eu-west-1. also the dynamodb table for locking is tf-locks-dev, put it in there too.\n\nthen run terraform init and it will ask you if you want to copy the state to the new backend, say yes. if it doesnt ask you use -migrate-state. then run terraform plan and it should say no changes, if it shows changes then something is wrong dont apply.\n\nyou need aws creds for the dev account with access to the bucket otherwise init fails with access denied, ask in platform channel for the role. after its working you can delete the local state file but wait a few days to be safe. also commit the backend.tf change in a PR.\n\nif the lock is stuck you can use force-unlock but be careful."}
